Tapping a live/finished card records the score block's First rect (lib/flip.ts,
Web Animations API, no dependency); the detail hero's score row — the Last
frame — plays the 300ms inversion (translate + scale + fade) out of that rect
once it mounts. One tap = one play: the rect is consumed on read and a ref
guards replays across refetches. Runs after two frames so the page-in wrapper
has committed its layout, and prefers-reduced-motion skips the animation
entirely. Cards with no score yet (scheduled) simply navigate without it.

